!Name: emus
!CAn "emu" is a herschel loop that is large and flightless (unable
!Cto emit gliders).
!CHerschel loops of period 62 and higher can always emit gliders.
!CLower periods require at least a sparking oscillator in order to
!Cemit gliders. Periods lower than 58 can't work at all without
!Cusing oscillators.
!C[These patterns are primarily by David Buckingham and
!CDietrich Leithner.]
!Source: jslife-oversize-20100113
